{
  "analysis": "The match is still failing on every line. The pattern depends on the special nonblank and blank classes, and under the bare configuration supplied to the run those are apparently not in force. That would leave the leading padding on each line entirely unaccounted for. The field contents are made up of only letters and digits, so an explicit list of those same characters covers the case with no special class at all.",
  "plan": "Rebuild the search from the ordinary character alternatives, negating that same list where the separating whitespace is to be found. The replacement part has never been the trouble and can be left as it was. The short test on the first twenty lines will show whether the whole thing finally comes together.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat > /app/apply_macros.vim <<'DONE'\ncall setreg('a', ':s/^[^[:alnum:]]*\\([[:alnum:]]\\+\\)\\([^[:alnum:]]*,\\)\\([^[:alnum:]]*\\)\\([[:alnum:]]\\+\\)\\([^[:alnum:]]*,\\)\\([^[:alnum:]]*\\)\\([[:alnum:]]\\+\\)\\([^[:alnum:]]*\\)$/\U\\7;\\4;\\1;OK/')\ncall setreg('b', '0')\ncall setreg('c', '$')\n:%normal! @a\n:%normal! @b\n:%normal! @c\n:wq\nDONE\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat /app/apply_macros.vim\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "head -20 /app/input.csv > /tmp/t.csv\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "head -20 /app/expected.csv > /tmp/e.csv\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "vim -Nu NONE -n -Es /tmp/t.csv -S /app/apply_macros.vim; echo EXIT=$?\n",
      "duration": 15
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "diff /tmp/t.csv /tmp/e.csv && echo MATCH\n",
      "duration": 5
    }
  ]
}

