steps.reasoning_content:
The trial on the short sample has once more been brought to a close, and the showing of the result is to be found to be in no way such as was to be looked for. The matter remains in the very same condition in which it was before the operation. That is to be traced to the circumstance that the character which is to be of the most essential use has not been able to get into the way in the form that is to be in any way of service. It is not to be supposed in the least that any further trial made in the same manner is to have the least chance of being of any use.

The only thing that remains open is that of making trial of that different manner in which the matter may be supplied in the form that is to be in a position to act. That fresh trial being made upon the same short sample is to be looked for to show in the end in what way the matter is to be brought about. When that shall have been found out the further course of the affair is to be based upon it. In that manner the whole of the matter may in the end be brought about in the form that has been in question from the very first of all.

The fresh direction is to be put in its way in the first place by the use of that sort of device that is to be found to be free from the difficulty that has been in the way in the course of the whole of the affair. When that is found to be of the kind that is to be looked for the further proceeding may be safely carried on in the same way to the accomplishment of the final end that has been in question. The hope is that in that way the whole of the matter is to be put to the close that has been in view.

